{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs",
  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_use_traversals_retained_selection_without_relisting]/impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]/fn[render]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "The agent asks only for outgoing edges and submits without reading\n contents. Its renderer is required by the agent interface, but any\n rendering would imply an unwanted content input. Other agent tests\n exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `render` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` (`fn[agent_edge_tools_use_traversals_retained_selection_without_relisting]/impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]/fn[render]`) is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Placement:** It is a fenced citation with commentary on an explicit function that has a body. That is a form the built-in permits, and it excuses only this function's zero execution.\n- **The reason is substantive and matches the source.**\n  - The test script has the agent make one `outgoing_edges` call and then `submit_result`. It never calls `read_node`.\n  - `validate` for node 1 calls `ctx.ask::<bool>()` with no content insertions. In `Ask::execute` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs`, the renderer is called only inside the insertion loop, which is empty here.\n  - In `Conversation::dispatch` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs`, the renderer is called only in the `read_node` arm. The `outgoing_edges` arm never calls it.\n  - So the renderer is required by the `AgentInputRenderer` interface but is correctly never reached. If it ran, that would be an unwanted content read, and the `panic!` makes that a failure.\n- **Other tests cover rendering:** The `Renderer` and `DistinctPages` implementations of `AgentInputRenderer<Memory>` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` return real contents. They cover the rendering path with explicitly requested contents, as the commentary says.\n\nThe citation gives a specific reason, not just difficulty, and I found no gap.",
